[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
OpenSearch Dashboards 2.17.1 runs here on the Node.js 24 of the package node24,
not on the Node.js 18 it was made for (at its end of life since 30.04.2025).

There is no security plugin (%%OSD_PLUGINS_OUT%%) in this package: OpenSearch
Dashboards talks to OpenSearch over plain http without credentials
(opensearch.hosts, default http://localhost:9200). The rc script refuses to start
with a setting of that plugin in %%ETCDIR%%/opensearch_dashboards.yml
(%%OSD_CONFIG_OUT%%): OpenSearch Dashboards would stop at its start on it. Without
the security plugin everyone who reaches its port can do everything: keep it
behind a firewall or a proxy with authentication.

The options of Node.js (--max-old-space-size and the like) go into
%%ETCDIR%%/node.options, one per line. Its log is rolled at 10 MB without
archives by newsyslog (%%PREFIX%%/etc/newsyslog.conf.d/opensearch_dashboards.conf);
service opensearch-dashboards reload opens it again. Its tools
(bin/opensearch-dashboards-plugin and -keystore in %%WWWDIR%%) stop as root
without --allow-root, as upstream.

Stop the service before this package replaces the official one: this rc script
keeps its pid file in /var/run/opensearch_dashboards/, the official one in
/var/run/opensearch_dashboards.pid (if that one still runs:
kill `cat /var/run/opensearch_dashboards.pid`).
EOM
}
]
